\paragraph{F6: $\dt{=}1$ imagination does not prevent all collapse.}
Exp\_008e\_v3 restricts imagination to $\dt{=}1$ while retaining the trained embedding. Two of four seeds collapse (50\%) via qualitatively distinct mechanisms: Pathway~A (seed~3, CIVO with entropy decrease, $\nve = 4.02\times$, eval 92.7) and Pathway~B (seed~2, entropy \emph{increase}, $\nve = 3.78\times$, eval 137.0). The remaining seeds are healthy (eval 870--899). The bimodal outcome reveals multiple independent vulnerability mechanisms (Figure~\ref{fig:multiple_pathways}; Appendix~\ref{sec:pathways}). Pathway~B produces the sole non-CIVO false positive in the NVE classification.

\paragraph{F7: Full-pathway gradient stopping shows mixed results.}
Full-SGS (exp\_018) detaches all non-KL gradients from $e_{\dt}$. Seed~1 avoids collapse (eval \sgseval{}) while seed~2 collapses (eval 40.8); recovery rate is 50\% (Figure~\ref{fig:civo_decomposition}; Appendix~\ref{sec:sgs_gradient_analysis}). Reward-only SGS (016e) fails entirely (NVE $10.42\times$), confirming that gradient importance and magnitude are decoupled. Cross-environment validation on Cheetah Run (010b, 2 seeds) confirms CIVO generalization (peak NVE $8.27\times$, $108.52\times$; collapse to eval 51.7, 0.83). Full-SGS on Cheetah enables recovery (eval 221.5 vs.\ permanent collapse without SGS). Removing the embedding eliminates CIVO entirely on Cheetah (024b, 2 seeds, NVE $< 0.2\times$), replicating the Walker causal control (008f).

